SPLIT X:BF-M1-0106 | a@194-197: 502 only when this API is an intermediary receiving an invalid upstream response; not every dependency failure. | b@199-204: 503 when the service is temporarily unable to handle the request, with Retry-After when a meaningful retry time is known. | c@206-212: 504 only for an upstream timeout when this API is an intermediary; distinguish client cancellation, own timeouts and upstream timeouts. | d@214-221: Repeated POSTs that must not duplicate effects may use an Idempotency-Key; key reuse with a different payload is 409; idempotency is not claimed merely because duplicates are unlikely. | e@223-236: When HTTP-level optimistic concurrency is part of the contract prefer standard conditional semantics (ETag, If-Match, 412) and do not replace them with custom status codes.
